{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MarkovTraceFactorization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MarkovTraceFactorization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.markov_trace_factorization_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.markov_trace_factorization_mul","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L165-L176","doc":"Wenzl disjoint-multiplicativity (the MonoidHom property of the Markov trace):\nthe traced-volume product over a concatenation of chains factors as the product\nof the two traced-volume products. This is `tr_M(K ⊔ K') = tr_M(K)·tr_M(K')`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.markov_trace_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.markov_trace_factorization","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L147-L152","doc":"Top-level alias matching the manifest declaration. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:markov-trace-factorization","label":"thm:markov-trace-factorization","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.invariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.invariance","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L144-L144","doc":"The trace is a link invariant (independent of braid representative).\nThis follows from the composition:\nOcneanu trace ∘ Gröbner reduction ∘ Hecke quotient\nwhere each step preserves the link invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.trace","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L136-L136","doc":"The Markov trace (product of traced volumes). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.chains_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.chains_length","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L134-L134","doc":"The list has the right length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.chains","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.chains","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L132-L132","doc":"Chain coefficients (a_i, b_i) for i = 0,...,A-2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.A","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L130-L130","doc":"Mass number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.n","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L128-L128","doc":"Number of neutrons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.p","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L126-L126","doc":"Number of protons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L124-L124","doc":"q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.q","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L122-L122","doc":"Substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L120-L120","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearTraceFactorization","kind":"structure","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L112-L145","doc":"The factorization of the link invariant through the Hecke algebra.\n\nEach step preserves the invariant:\n1. Braid → Hecke: quotient by Skein ideal (well-defined on links)\n2. Hecke → Chain: Gröbner reduction (confluence / diamond lemma)\n3. Chain → Trace: Markov property (link invariant by Ocneanu)\n4. Product: the factorization theorem (this file) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingMixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingMixed","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L102-L106","doc":"Mixed crossing (proton-neutron): c = 1, d = -(q - q⁻¹)/2, the average\nof the positive and negative crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingNegative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingNegative","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L93-L100","doc":"Negative crossing (neutron-neutron): c = 1, d = -(q - q⁻¹), i.e.\n`σ_i - (q - q⁻¹) = σ_i⁻¹` by the Hecke relation. Matches the (c, d)\ntable of this block, `nucleon_typed_d` in `inverse-markov-qvalues.py`\nand `crossingNN` in `generator-volume-decomposition.lean`. (Corrected\n2026-11-16 from a convention-C form `(q², -q(√q - 1/√q))`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingPositive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingPositive","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L89-L91","doc":"Positive crossing (proton-proton): c = 1, d = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.asymptoticRatio_at_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.asymptoticRatio_at_q","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L78-L83","doc":"Numerical verification: at q = 1.1097, the asymptotic ratio ≈ 10.116. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.asymptoticRatio_eq_inv_hbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.asymptoticRatio_eq_inv_hbar","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L70-L76","doc":"The asymptotic ratio equals 1/ℏ_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.asymptoticRatio_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.asymptoticRatio_pos","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L62-L68","doc":"The asymptotic ratio is positive for q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.asymptoticRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.asymptoticRatio","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L54-L60","doc":"The asymptotic ratio: tr(L_0)/tr(parent) → 1/ℏ_q as A → ∞.\n\nFor heavy nuclei, the L_0 trace converges to 1/ℏ_q times\nthe parent trace, where ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tracedVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tracedVolume","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L46-L52","doc":"The Markov-traced generator volume: V̂_i = z · a_i + b_i.\n\nThis is the contribution of generator σ_i to the total\nMarkov trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.chebyshevStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.chebyshevStep","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L35-L44","doc":"The Chebyshev transfer matrix at one crossing.\n\nGiven current state (a, b) representing a σ_i + b,\nand crossing coefficients (c, d) representing c σ_i + d,\nthe product (a σ + b)(c σ + d) reduces via σ² = (q-q⁻¹)σ + 1 to:\n  a' = ac(q-q⁻¹) + ad + bc\n  b' = ac + bd ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.markovZ","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-factorization.lean#L30-L33","doc":"The Markov trace parameter z = q³/(q²+1) (convention D). ","signatureChunk":0}]}